          "text": "Description: On November 1, 1981, around 11 a.m., several witnesses spotted a flying object slowly heading towards the sea. This gray, cylindrical object was approximately 4 meters long. No noise was heard during the object's movement. The investigation will reveal that it was a promotional balloon launched by children from the terrace of the \"Le Corbusier\" building, about 300 meters from the observation location.",
